From 1192b995c28f7984edb50e871b6a89778fafe069 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 03:40:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix F90-F93: order-stream exit dispatch, trail SL binding,
 spot gate, rate-limit alert
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Four verified correctness defects found by auditing the orchestrator and trail
engine against actual code paths (DOX rule 2 — comments are not ground truth).
No strategy semantics changed; all four are crash / dead-code / silent-freeze
defects. F-numbers continue the in-file registry per DOX rule 15.

F90 (CRITICAL) _handle_order_stream_event priority-2 exit branch dereferenced
  five attributes OptionsBuyerEdgeBot does not own (_pending_tranche_exits{,_lock},
  journal, _finalize_exit, _notify) — all live on OrderManager. AST ownership
  check confirms the orchestrator has no bases and defines none of them. Every
  streamed exit fill raised AttributeError, was swallowed by the _strategy_thread
  catch-all, and aborted the rest of that cycle. Latent only because
  order_updates_enabled defaults FALSE. Routed through self.orders.* /
  self._send_alert.

F91 (HIGH) _process_premium_trail left _lock_floor unbound on the
  non-ATR + tgt <= entry_premium path, then read it — UnboundLocalError confirmed
  by execution. Reachable via PREMIUM_TARGET_PTS=0 (unvalidated) and via startup
  restore overwriting pos.tgt from a broker LIMIT guarded only by > 0. Sibling
  code already carries a sentinel for this exact state (L4333). Bound to ep.

F92 (HIGH) check_trailing_stops computed _needs_spot, then unconditionally gated
  on a redundant spot_ltp recompute, defeating it. Premium trail takes no spot
  argument (AST-verified), so in the DEFAULT config a stale spot feed silently
  froze the trail with no [DATA-MISS] log. Gate moved into the two spot-consuming
  branches only.

F93 (MEDIUM) fetch_quote rate-limit alert guarded on hasattr() for an attribute
  set in __init__ — always True, so the alert could never fire. Also violated the
  file's own CODING CONVENTIONS ban on lazy hasattr. Matches sibling auth branch.

Registered but deliberately NOT applied:
F94 (HIGH) session-aware min_score never reaches StrikeSelector / conviction
  scalars. Measured: power hour scores 32-39 pass EXECUTE then get rejected by
  select_best and fall through to simple_otm (no delta targeting, no quality
  gate); morning gate overstates conviction 3.3x, relaxing the asym gate exactly
  when discipline should tighten. Patch ready; deferred under the same rule as
  F83 — live trade-selection parameters are not changed without explicit review.
F95 (research) _compute_oi_wall has no +1 branch, a standing directional skew.
  Scoring-model gap, not a coding defect — belongs to CALIBRATION / RESEARCH.

Verified: py_compile OK, pyflakes clean, AST undefined-attribute sweep clean,
branch-coverage execution of the _lock_floor and trail-dispatch paths.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018ohYuXf53pGPhTWo6kGxEJ
